<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Friedrich Hecker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1811">1811</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Friedrich Hecker was a lawyer and radical democrat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> who led an armed rising for a German republic in April 1848, the Hecker Uprising, which was defeated near Kandern. He fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> and then to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where he farmed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> and served as a colonel in the Union army during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/friedrich-hecker.jpg" alt="Friedrich Hecker" width="200" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fr_Hecker_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
